---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Mobility and Recovery After Workouts';
const description = 'A guide to mobility and recovery after workouts, including body care routines, stretching, breathing and recovery habits.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Recovery</div><h1>Mobility and recovery after workouts.</h1><p class="lead">Recovery is not a luxury. It is part of the training plan. The right mobility and body care work can help people move better, feel better and stay consistent.</p></div></section>
<section class="content"><div class="container"><article>

<h2>What recovery actually means</h2><p>Recovery is the process that helps the body adapt after training. It includes sleep, nutrition, hydration, stress management, light movement and mobility work.</p><h2>When to do mobility work</h2><p>Mobility and body care can be done after training, on rest days or during short breaks. The goal is not to force flexibility. The goal is to restore comfortable movement and reduce unnecessary tension.</p><h2>Helpful recovery routine structure</h2><ul><li>Start with breathing to bring the body down after training.</li><li>Use gentle mobility for hips, shoulders, spine and ankles.</li><li>Include light activation work if certain areas feel inactive.</li><li>Keep the routine short enough to repeat consistently.</li><li>Pair recovery with protein, hydration and quality sleep.</li></ul><h2>How an app can help</h2><p>Most users skip recovery because they are not sure what to do. A guided body care section gives users a clear plan after training or on rest days.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Content angle:</strong> This page should connect the topic back to the app naturally. Mention guided training, body care, nutrition education and mental performance where relevant without forcing a sales pitch.</div>
</article></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
